  "reason": "Harness activity cost fixes (HARN-7, HARN-8, HARN-9, HARN-11). Assistant message deltas are coalesced like command output, so replay, follow and stopped-answer semantics are covered by test_harness_activity_cost.py (new: row bound, live == replay == saved, stream separation, Stop inside the window, late plan/goal/mode past 1,000 events and behind 1,001 older turns, incremental decode counts, conversation-scoped message reads, signal-woken followers for completed and interrupted turns, stdlib-only shim, entry dispatch without Core imports, stdio round trip through the real launch command, frozen unpack-env forwarding), test_harnesses.py (runtime streaming, session activity, gateway launch), test_harness_stopped_turns.py and test_harness_leftovers.py (stop/interrupt and coalescer lifecycle), test_chat_reconnection.py, test_approval_handoff.py and test_approval_continuation.py (followers and message_delta progress after decisions), the vendor turn files (Claude, Codex, Grok, commands, adapters, vendor session recreate, subagent choice, provider subagents, chat goals) that stream through stream_turn/start_chat_turn, test_storage.py and test_row_horizon.py (filtered replay_operation_events, last_operation_event_sequence, the one-page lookup guard), and test_mcp_gateway.py, test_cli.py and test_packaging.py (shim client, hidden CLI command, bundled shim audit and build script).",
  "exclusions": "Full suites are not approved and are excluded. Seven test functions (nine nodes) are pre-existing failures on origin/main, verified on a pristine worktree, and are excluded by node selection: test_harnesses.py::test_harness_gateway_lists_scoped_sources_with_url_metadata, ::test_browser_gateway_rechecks_conversation_binding_before_execution and ::test_workspace_retrieval_reports_actionable_argument_errors (x3; they expect raised HarnessConfigurationError that is now returned as a tool result); test_harness_provider_subagents.py::test_operator_limit_reaches_the_harness_and_is_enforced, ::test_harness_answers_a_subagent_question_with_subagent_message and ::test_harness_gets_unread_subagent_messages_at_its_next_turn; test_packaging.py::test_nebula3_runtime_has_no_conditional_import_fallbacks (flags vault_probe.py). test_api.py and test_chat_api.py are not selected: test_api.py monkeypatches follow_turn and its session-activity test covers the chat-level route in session_state.py, which is unchanged; test_chat_api.py covers the same chat-level activity. No frontend, native or Playwright tests: nothing under ui/ or Rust changed and the harness activity, events and session-activity response shapes are unchanged; mocked Playwright cannot observe these server-side costs, and the real-Core harness journey needs vendor binaries CI lacks, so it was run locally against scratch and packaged Cores (see PR body).",
